win32u: OpenGL in windows through the surfaceless EGL driver (no Wayland EGL on Haiku)

Mesa on Haiku has no Wayland EGL platform, so Wine's OpenGL uses win32u's own
EGL driver on the surfaceless platform. Its window drawable (an emulated
framebuffer) had two gaps for the Raspberry Pi 4: it was built with OpenGL
4.5's direct state access, which an OpenGL 2.1 driver (Mesa's V3D) does not
have — no framebuffer was ever made — and nothing showed a finished frame in
the window. The framebuffer is now made with the OpenGL 3.0 /
ARB_framebuffer_object calls (keeping the caller's bindings), and a swap (or a
flush of a single-buffered window) reads the frame back and draws it into the
window's DC as a DIB.
